          "id": "http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416",
          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "TL 10 NW                    REDBOURN             HOGG END LANE                                                  (north side) 9/219                                            Nos 1 and 3 Beech Hyde                                                  Cottage II Pair of houses, formerly one large farmhouse.  C16 timber frame, extended away from road with a gabled mid-C17 wing.  Further extended c.1800.  C20 rear extension, possibly  incorporating early timber frame.  Exposed framing to early part;  C17 wing red brick with stone quoins.  Plain tile roofs. Early part is 3 bays with 3 C20 glazing bar casements.  Circa 1600 ridge chimney stack, the roof line higher to left and right, possibly a hall in this position.   C17 wing has floor band and wide 3-light casement.  Circa 1800 block has good doorcase with moulded panels and reveals.  Leaded fan with husk swags.  Plain pilasters with dentilled capitals.  Dentilled and modillioned open pediment.   2 C19/20 glazing bar casements,  the one next to the door with segmental head.  Dentilled brick eaves.  Low slate roof. Listing NGR: TL1111008908"
    }
  ],
